<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nonantola Abbey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">752</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nonantola Abbey is a Benedictine monastery near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, founded in 752 by Anselm, a former Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friuli">Friuli</a> and brother-in-law of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aistulf">Aistulf</a>. Favoured by Lombard and Carolingian rulers, it grew into one of the richest abbeys of Italy, with a renowned scriptorium. Its Romanesque church dates from the 12th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nonantola-abbey.jpg" alt="Nonantola Abbey" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: sailko · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abbazia_di_nonantola_00.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
